{
  "anonymous_report": "**Publish the tenfold claim for total volume, not for yield per square mile.** During May 1–31, 2023, the Potomac at Little Falls carried **424.45 times** as much water as the Northwest Branch Anacostia near Hyattsville. Its drainage area was about 234 times as large, so its gauged volume per square mile was only **1.81 times** that of the Northwest Branch.\n\n| USGS gauge | May volume (billion L) | Drainage area (mi²) | May yield (million L/mi²) |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| Potomac River at Little Falls Pump Station (01646500) | 840.105 | 11,560 | 72.67 |\n| Northwest Branch Anacostia River near Hyattsville (01651000) | 1.97928 | 49.4 | 40.07 |\n\nBoth gauges had approved USGS daily mean discharge values on **all 31 dates**, with no gaps. Each monthly volume is the sum of those daily means multiplied by 86,400 seconds per day and converted to liters. Yield is that volume divided by the station inventory’s reported drainage area (`drain_area_va`).\n\n**Neither verdict changes under the desk’s ±5% flow scenario.** With drainage areas fixed, lowering Potomac flow by 5% and raising Northwest Branch flow by 5% gives the minimum ratio; reversing the changes gives the maximum. The total-volume ratio ranges from **384.03 to 469.13**, always above ten. The per-square-mile ratio ranges from **1.641 to 2.005**, always below ten. These are sensitivity bounds, not USGS error estimates.",
  "criteria": {
    "areas": "Uses both NWIS drainage areas with the correct units and matches them to the right station IDs.",
    "normalized": "Computes the larger-to-smaller area-specific ratio within 1% and correctly disposes of the second tenfold claim.",
    "provenance_and_limits": "Cites daily-value and station-area records separately; bounds conclusion to the observed month and avoids unsupported hydrological causes or long-term generalization.",
    "raw_claim": "Evaluates the draft’s tenfold raw-volume threshold with the correct numerator, denominator, ratio and direction.",
    "sensitivity": "Evaluates independent ±5% flow perturbations for both ratios or supplies mathematically equivalent limits, and labels this a desk scenario.",
    "sites_time": "Identifies both records, directions and the May 1–31 2023 common window (31 approved daily means each).",
    "volume": "Monthly common-support totals for both stations match the original records and declared units within 1%."
  },
